course: dictionary
lesson: 8047
title: Growing back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To regrow means to grow again after something has been cut, lost or damaged. The little word re- at the start means again, so regrow means grow again. Look for re- at the start of a word to spot this clue.
explain: «Lizards can regrow their tails» tells you that a lizard's tail can grow back after it is lost. «Regrow a forest» means to make a forest grow again after it has been cut down.
explain: Context gives you the clues. «A sea star has no brain, can regrow a lost arm.» The word lost tells you that regrow means growing back the part that went missing.
fact: Regrow is a verb, so its forms are regrow, regrows, regrew, regrown and regrowing.
fact: «Regrow» means to grow again after being cut, lost or damaged.
fact: «A sea star» can regrow a lost arm.
fact: «An axolotl» can regrow a whole lost leg, with bones, muscles and nerves, and it leaves no scar.
fact: Hair and nails regrow, but adult teeth do not regrow once they are lost.
exercise: «A sea star has no brain, can regrow a lost arm.» What does regrow mean here? | To cut off a limb | To run very fast | *To grow again after being lost | To hide under a rock
exercise: «Grass regrows 2 cm a week.» How much does the grass grow each week? | *2 cm | 12 cm | 2 m | 20 cm
exercise: In regrow, the first part re- means what? | Away | Very | Under | *Again
test: «An axolotl can regrow a whole lost leg.» What did the axolotl do with its lost leg? | To swim away from it | *Grew a new one | To hide it under the water | To paint it a new colour
test: «Hair and nails regrow, but adult teeth do not.» Which is true? | Hair never regrows | *Adult teeth do not regrow | Nails do not grow at all | Teeth regrow in the same way as hair
exam: Which statement about regrow is correct? | Regrow means to cut something off | Regrow is a noun for a plant | *Regrow means to grow again after being cut, lost or damaged | A starfish can regrow a lost arm
